WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:05.370
Hey Youtubers it's Charlie and Marvel is getting
ready to announce the Director of the Doctor

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:08.750
Strange movie. Which pretty much confirms
it's going to be one of those mystery Phase

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:15.080
3 movies. The director is Scott Derrickson
who did this really creepy horror movie The

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:20.789
Exorcism of Emily Rose and Sinister with Ethan
Hawke. That doesn't mean Ethan Hawke is going

00:00:20.789 --> 00:00:25.430
to be Doctor Strange, but this video will
be my Top 10 picks for who it should be.

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:29.410
Just as an update on Ant-Man, they haven't
found a new director yet, but the frontrunner

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:34.409
is Rawson Thurber, he's the guy who directed
Dodgeball. If you're finding me for the first

00:00:34.409 --> 00:00:40.140
time, I do bonus Marvel and DC videos every
week. Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:45.969
There are links for my social accounts where
I post updates on what each video is going

00:00:45.969 --> 00:00:47.030
to be.

00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:51.280
So Doctor Strange, before we talk about actors,
we have to talk about what kind of a movie

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:57.339
this is going to be. It's not just going to
be Iron Man with Magic. The vibe of the comics

00:00:57.339 --> 00:01:00.969
will inform the vibe of the movie and the
person Marvel picks to play Doctor Strange.

00:01:00.969 --> 00:01:06.500
The character at his core has the same call
to action that Tony Stark does, but where

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:11.759
Iron Man is a story that revolves around technology
and transparency, Doctor Strange is a really

00:01:11.759 --> 00:01:17.369
Dark, Eerie exploration of the mind. And Demons,
lots of demons. Which kind of explains why

00:01:17.369 --> 00:01:20.799
they would pick a director that did movies
about demons.

00:01:20.799 --> 00:01:24.950
This has a real chance of being Marvel's first
big Horror Movie. and when I say Horror, I

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:30.119
mean Disney horror, not Eli Roth torture porn,
like Hostel. Imagine what that would look

00:01:30.119 --> 00:01:31.619
like.

00:01:31.619 --> 00:01:35.329
So when we think about actors we want to play
the role, we have to limit choices to people

00:01:35.329 --> 00:01:40.469
who can do really dark horror movies and come
out looking like an Iron Man level hero. Just

00:01:40.469 --> 00:01:44.670
look at him during Marvel's Infinity event
last year. I don't think he can even remember

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:49.259
the last time he smiled. Think about actors
who can make that kind of person appealing.

00:01:49.259 --> 00:01:54.549
So here are my top 10 picks for Doctor Strange.
Number 10 - Jon Hamm

00:01:54.549 --> 00:01:59.149
I feel like Jon Hamm is being considered for
every major troubled hero of a certain age.

00:01:59.149 --> 00:02:03.109
He's done with Mad Men, even though they still
have 7 more episodes to air next year. They've

00:02:03.109 --> 00:02:08.319
shot everything. So he's free to do more movies
now. Without making too many Don Draper analogies,

00:02:08.319 --> 00:02:14.050
Hamm has been really good at making an unlikable
character very appealing. Stephen Strange

00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:16.950
is a way bigger asshole than Tony Stark.

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:21.370
When he becomes Doctor Strange he's full on
zen. Which almost looks like the absence of

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:26.530
emotion. I'm just picturing that cold Don
Draper stare while he's whispering a spell.

00:02:26.530 --> 00:02:28.590
Number 9 - Justin Theroux

00:02:28.590 --> 00:02:32.800
He was rumored for the role a long time ago
and like Jon Hamm, he's played some darker

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:37.530
roles. He's got a strong comedy background,
but even the funny characters he's played

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:40.080
are super dark or downright evil.

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:42.500
He doesn't quite have the A-List appeal of
someone like Jon Hamm or some of the other

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:47.370
guys on my list, but I think he's a little
more versatile. There can be no Marvel film

00:02:47.370 --> 00:02:51.730
without a little bit of humor. So just being
really depressing and good looking isn't going

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:52.810
to be enough.

00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:58.290
The only thing that might keep him from doing
it is his new HBO series The Leftovers. He's

00:02:58.290 --> 00:03:02.560
one of the stars. It's a Damon Lindelof Series
too with pretty good reviews. So I don't see

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:06.400
him dumping that for a Marvel Movie, but never
say never.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:07.940
Number 8 - Kit Harington

00:03:07.940 --> 00:03:12.330
One of two Game of Thrones actors on my list.
He's only just started to break out with some

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:17.000
big budget movies, but he's got the appeal
Marvel and Disney want for a movie this big.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:22.030
And because he's relatively new they can get
him on the cheap. A opposed to someone like

00:03:22.030 --> 00:03:24.390
Johnny Depp who's super expensive.

00:03:24.390 --> 00:03:28.930
He's booked a movie in 2015 already, which
may or may not cause some schedule conflicts,

00:03:28.930 --> 00:03:31.840
but if he can shoot other big movies and do
Game of Thrones at the same time. There's

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:36.500
no reason he couldn't shoot a Marvel movie.

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:41.310
Just for reference too, the unofficial release
date for the Doctor Strange movie is May 5th

00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:46.620
2017. Which means they'd have to start shooting
it early in 2015. Most big movies like this

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:51.440
and Avengers 2 shoot about a year and a half
to two years in advance of their release dates.

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:56.350
That two year period after is what it usually
takes to do the special effects.

00:03:56.350 --> 00:03:58.060
Number 7 - Hugh Laurie

00:03:58.060 --> 00:04:01.860
This is an unlikely choice but I feel like
he would be so good for the part I had to

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:06.870
put him on my list. He's starring as the villain
in Brad Bird's Tomorrowland movie, which is

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:13.870
also Disney. It's scheduled for release May
22, 2017. I don't see Disney sticking a leading

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:17.230
actor in two of their films so close to each
other.

00:04:17.230 --> 00:04:22.660
I would really like to see a slightly more
British version of Doctor House become sorcerer

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:23.680
supreme.

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:26.890
Number 6 - Keanu Reeves

00:04:26.890 --> 00:04:30.930
He's gotten typecast in roles that are either
really heavy on psychology or supernatural

00:04:30.930 --> 00:04:35.830
forces. But that's only because he can play
that flat dark emotion so well. I know a lot

00:04:35.830 --> 00:04:39.950
of people give him crap for looking like he
doesn't act at all, but I think he'd be able

00:04:39.950 --> 00:04:44.750
to pull of the Doctor Strange persona very
well. It's the Stephen Strange part I think

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:49.640
he'd have more trouble with. He does a lot
better when his characters aren't too intense,

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:54.300
like during Constantine when he's giving Rachel
Weisz the business about angels and demons.

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:56.620
Like he's so tired of everything, as if it's
no big deal.

00:04:56.620 --> 00:04:58.120
Number 5 - Aiden Gillen

00:04:58.120 --> 00:05:01.990
My other Game of Thrones actor on the list.
I feel like Littlefinger would make a great

00:05:01.990 --> 00:05:06.730
Doctor Strange. Imagine a slightly less evil
version of Baelish, less pathology. He doesn't

00:05:06.730 --> 00:05:11.830
look like someone who could open a 150 Million
Dollar Movie, but he's played so many amazing

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:16.750
dark characters so well I feel like he would
be a welcome addition to the Avengers roster.

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:21.980
When you look at them, the Hulk is really
the darkest character. But the Doctor Strange

00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:28.700
persona is almost noir and Gillen has that
edge to him that Mark Ruffalo doesn't. Ruffalo

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:35.700
is just too adorable. I feel like Doctor Strange
can't just be a super handsome, typically

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:40.980
Hollywood looking actor. Which kind of explains
my next picks.

00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:43.160
Number 4 - Viggo Mortensen

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:47.220
He's got the charisma to lead a big movie
Aragorn style, but he's someone that has a

00:05:47.220 --> 00:05:51.950
really easy time disappearing into characters.
Meaning when we see him on screen we don't

00:05:51.950 --> 00:05:58.950
think about Viggo, we think about the character
he's playing. That's another Johnny Depp problem,

00:06:00.639 --> 00:06:06.990
which is why I think Marvel is going to find
an actor like Viggo who can go really dark

00:06:06.990 --> 00:06:11.900
and still be charismatic without bringing
a ton of 'hollywood actor' baggage.

00:06:11.900 --> 00:06:17.330
Plus, currently he hasn't booked any movies
beyond this year. So he's totally available.

00:06:17.330 --> 00:06:22.169
And relatively affordable. The only issue
I see is that he'd have to sign the same 6

00:06:22.169 --> 00:06:26.320
picture deal Marvel makes all of it's actors
sign. And I don't know if he'd want to commit

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:30.330
to something for the 8 plus years it would
take to fulfill that contract.

00:06:30.330 --> 00:06:33.940
Even Chris Evans is ready to be doing other
things and he's only finished about half of

00:06:33.940 --> 00:06:34.440
his contract.

00:06:34.440 --> 00:06:36.740
Number 3 - Mads Mikkelsen

00:06:36.740 --> 00:06:41.290
Anyone who watches Hannibal will understand
how amazing Mads is. Yes, he's a really really

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:46.010
awful guy on that show. But he has this very
subtle way about him that makes you both terrified

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:51.720
and hypnotized by him at the same time. Which
I think is what Marvel will want for Strange.

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:56.650
When you look at pictures like this, you can
clearly see how scary he looks despite being

00:06:56.650 --> 00:06:58.020
a force for good.

00:06:58.020 --> 00:07:02.760
You could almost say that Mads plays a food
magician on Hannibal. Even if he uses people

00:07:02.760 --> 00:07:08.580
meats. But who else thinks that a Marvel hero
that scares the crap out of you would be amazing?

00:07:08.580 --> 00:07:11.300
Number 2 - Benedict Cumberbatch

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:15.260
Probably one of the most in demand actors
in the world right now. His Sherlock character

00:07:15.260 --> 00:07:20.610
is a good analog for Stephen Strange. A hyper
kinetic genius with a lot of pathos. He's

00:07:20.610 --> 00:07:25.590
even starring in an animated movie called
Magik coming out July 4th 2016.

00:07:25.590 --> 00:07:30.370
As much as I could argue why he's got all
the qualities I think make a perfect Doctor

00:07:30.370 --> 00:07:36.560
Strange, I feel like his fans will just hear
Magic Sherlock. Which I don't think Marvel

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:42.610
would mind at all. A lot of who they cast
will depend on the Director. So as long as

00:07:42.610 --> 00:07:47.870
Derrickson feels like Cumberbatch would fit
in one of his movies it's perfect.

00:07:47.870 --> 00:07:52.110
Scheduling issues would be the only thing
that could kill this. They already had to

00:07:52.110 --> 00:07:55.800
delay Sherlock Series 4 for two years because
he and Martin Freeman were so busy. Signing

00:07:55.800 --> 00:07:59.290
up for 6 Marvel movies might not be something
he'd want to do.

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:03.330
But, giant asterisk. He did say he really
wanted to be a part of the new Star Wars movies

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:07.729
as a Jedi and that didn't quite work out.
So there is a precedent for him gravitating

00:08:07.729 --> 00:08:09.310
towards these giant franchises.

00:08:09.310 --> 00:08:13.260
and my Number 1 pick for Doctor Strange - Daniel
Bruhl

00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:17.930
This might not be a guy you've seen or heard
of, but he's been a favorite of critics recently

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:22.650
in big movies like Rush, Inglorious Bastards
and Bourne Ultimatum. You do really need to

00:08:22.650 --> 00:08:26.810
check him out in Rush. He plays exactly the
kind of anti-hero you would find in a Marvel

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:32.070
movie and he's got the benefit of being relatively
new. I think of his career as being a lot

00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:35.769
like Mark Ruffalo's in that they've both done
some big movies but they're not like Robert

00:08:35.769 --> 00:08:39.539
Downey Jr, their careers are still rising.
Downey on the other hand is at his peak. He

00:08:39.539 --> 00:08:40.610
can't really go any higher.

00:08:40.610 --> 00:08:45.660
Bruhl has this crazy intensity that I think
in combination with his appeal and availability

00:08:45.660 --> 00:08:47.829
would make an amazing Doctor Strange.

00:08:47.829 --> 00:08:51.350
But now it's your turn, let me know who you
think should play Doctor Strange.

00:08:51.350 --> 00:08:56.920
They probably won't be doing a post-credits
scene for him in any of the movies for a long

00:08:56.920 --> 00:09:03.920
time, but the Character was part of The Defenders
which Marvel is doing on Netflix in a couple

00:09:04.369 --> 00:09:07.290
years. So that's probably where they'll debut
the character first.

00:09:07.290 --> 00:09:11.119
One of the biggest issues is that it has to
be the right actor at the right time and a

00:09:11.119 --> 00:09:15.619
lot of these people on my list book their
time years in advance. That's typically why

00:09:15.619 --> 00:09:19.959
most big actors drop out of movies, because
they overlap with other mega movies they want

00:09:19.959 --> 00:09:20.410
to make.

00:09:20.410 --> 00:09:26.360
A really good example is Emily Blunt, who
was originally supposed to be Black Widow.

00:09:26.360 --> 00:09:29.610
She had to turn down that role because of
a schedule conflict. I think we're all happy

00:09:29.610 --> 00:09:34.360
with Scarlett Johansson, but if you want to
see a badass Emily Blunt, go see Edge of Tomorrow

00:09:34.360 --> 00:09:37.990
this weekend. I'll be doing a review of that
on Thursday or Friday.

